rket share, and strengthen customer reach, with direct exports of rice and food products to various countries commencing. The Company has entered into a rent agreement at Kutch, Gujarat, where operations have not yet started as development is under process. Separately, the Company sold its Murthal unit to M/s. RCM Consumer Products Private Limited under a One Time Settlement.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"moat":{"title":"Strengths (RHP)","body":"brand: The 'Kohinoor' brand is a household name in export markets including the USA, UAE, Canada, Australia, the Middle East, Singapore, Japan and Mauritius — evidence: \"the most powerful brand of the Company 'Kohinoor' is a household name in the countries like USA, UAE, Canada, Australia, Middle East, Singapore, Japan, Mauritius & other European countries.\"","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"risks":{"title":"Risks (RHP)","body":"- The rice industry continues to remain inherently volatile, impacted by factors such as climate change, geopolitical uncertainty, fluctuating demand, and evolving trade dynamics.\n- Export markets remained subdued due to global economic uncertainty and operational limitations, affecting the Company's international sales.\n- The Company has faced financial constraints, economic pressures and liquidity challenges since 2017-18, requiring restructuring of operations and cost reduction measures.\n- The Company's Debt Equity Ratio is negative due to erosion of net worth because of losses, indicating a weakened financial position.\n- Interest Coverage Ratio and Operating Profit Margin are both negative because the Company has an operating loss.\n- Kohinoor Foods USA Inc. currently carries no business as there is no export sales for KFL India to US & Canada, and its office is closed due to no business.","src":"drhp","as_of":""},"strategy":{"title":"Strategies (RHP)","body":"- Expanding presence in global markets.\n- Expanding the product portfolio.\n- Expanding the customer base.\n- Leveraging market expertise and